  "id": "Compound::DB00860 - Disease::DOID:3083",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone, through its treatment of Asthma, may contribute to the pathogenesis of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) by influencing inflammatory processes in the airways. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone is linked to Asthma, which is then treated by various bronchodilators such as Tiotropium, Formoterol, and Arformoterol, all of which are capable of treating COPD. This implies a potential indirect pathway where Prednisolone's effects on Asthma could modulate the inflammatory response, potentially exacerbating COPD symptoms. The shared lowest common ancestor between Asthma and COPD, as well as the presence of multiple treatment pathways, suggests a broader network of interactions that may be relevant to the disease. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering both direct and indirect mechanisms in understanding the role of Prednisolone in COPD.",
